1. **`apps/web/src/cards/cards.css`, rule `:root:not([data-reduce-motion="true"]) .cf[data-foil="animated"]::after`** (inside `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)`, about line 1689). Change the two coloured stops of its `linear-gradient(90deg, …)` and add one declaration after the gradient's `);`, before `will-change: transform;`. The rule must end up exactly:
   ```css
     :root:not([data-reduce-motion="true"]) .cf[data-foil="animated"]::after {
       left: 0;
       width: 170%;
       background: linear-gradient(
         90deg,
         transparent 0%,
         rgb(255 244 200 / 0.2) 25%,
         transparent 46%,
         rgb(255 214 110 / 0.14) 73%,
         transparent 100%
       );
       mix-blend-mode: normal;
       will-change: transform;
       animation: cf-foil-sweep 8s linear infinite;
     }
   ```
   `mix-blend-mode: normal` is needed: the shared still rule above (`.cf[data-foil="static"]::after, .cf[data-foil="animated"]::after`) sets `overlay` on the same pseudo-element.

2. **Same file, rule `:root:not([data-reduce-motion="true"]) .cf[data-rarity="Mythic"][data-foil="animated"]::after`** (about line 1704). Change only the four alphas; the percentages stay:
   ```css
         rgb(255 106 213 / 0.16) 23%,
         rgb(148 208 255 / 0.16) 40%,
         rgb(125 255 198 / 0.14) 58%,
         rgb(255 230 109 / 0.14) 75%,
   ```
   Add no `mix-blend-mode` here; it inherits the cascade from step 1's rule.
   Every new alpha is 0.4 of the still band's (0.5→0.2, 0.35→0.14, 0.4→0.16). On the faces' dark panels, normal blending at that alpha lifts the backdrop about as much as `overlay` did at the full alpha. The planner rendered these exact values on gold and Mythic faces.

3. **Same file, the comment above the `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)` block** (the one that starts `/* The sweep (#200).`). Before its closing `*/`, add this paragraph, wrapped to match the lines around it:
   ```
   The sweep blends nothing (#1700). With `mix-blend-mode` on the layer the compositor moves,
   Chrome drew a dark wedge past a rotated face's rounded corner, and a dark strip along its edge,
   each time the band came in or left (the home screen's fan, rotated by landing.css); `screen`
   did the same. Drawn with plain alpha the band stays inside the clip, and the blend's extra pass
   per face per frame is gone. Its stops carry 0.4 of the still band's alpha, about the lift the
   overlay gave a dark panel. The still foil keeps its overlay: it never moves.
   ```
   Change no other comment or rule in the file.

4. **`apps/web/src/cards/foil.test.ts`, header comment.** After the line `// (game/animations.test.ts does the same for its sheet).` add:
   ```ts
   // #1700: the sweep composites with no blend mode, which on a rotated face (the home screen's
   // fan) drew a dark wedge past the rounded corner, and its band is lit at a share of the still
   // band's alpha instead.
   ```

5. **Same file, after the `gradients()` function** (before `describe(`), add:
   ```ts
   /** The alpha of every `rgb(… / a)` stop in `gradient`, in order. */
   function alphas(gradient: string): number[] {
     return [...gradient.matchAll(/\/\s*([\d.]+)\)/g)].map((match) => Number(match[1]));
   }

   /** The swept band's alpha as a share of the still band's at the same stop (#1700). */
   const SWEPT_ALPHA_SHARE = 0.4;
   ```

6. **Same file, inside `describe("the animated foil sweep", …)`, after the last `it`**, add the three tests in the **Tests** section below, exactly as written.

7. **`docs/polish/6-cards.md`, at the end of the file**, add a blank line, then:
   ```markdown
   ## Addendum: the foil sweep's corners (2026-10-23, #1700)

   The sweep #200 built still showed a seam on rotated faces. It is fixed in the card layer alone;
   no rule changed.

   - **A dark wedge at the corners.** The moving layer kept the still foil's `mix-blend-mode:
     overlay`. On a rotated face (every card of the home screen's fan) Chrome drew a dark wedge past
     the rounded corner, and a dark strip along the face's edge, as the band came in at the top left
     and left at the bottom right, which is where the loop restarts. Any blend mode did it (`screen`
     too), and none did it once the layer was composited without one.
   - **The sweep now blends nothing.** Its rule sets `mix-blend-mode: normal`, and its stops carry
     0.4 of the still band's alpha (gold 0.2 and 0.14, Mythic 0.16 and 0.14), about the lift the
     overlay gave a dark panel. The layer, its size, the 8 s loop and the keyframes are unchanged, so
     each face still costs one layer moved by `transform`, and the blend's extra pass per face per
     frame is gone (`cards/foil.test.ts`).
   - **The still foil keeps its overlay.** It never moves, so it is painted with the face, and the
     reduced-motion face that wears it is unchanged.
   ```

## Tests

File `apps/web/src/cards/foil.test.ts`, inside the existing `describe`. Each of these fails on `main` (the planner checked the regexes against `main`'s sheet and against a copy with steps 1–2 applied):

```ts
  it("composites the sweep with no blend mode, so a rotated face keeps its rounded corners (#1700)", () => {
    const animated = ruleBody(
      /:root:not\(\[data-reduce-motion="true"\]\) \.cf\[data-foil="animated"\]::after/,
    );
    expect(animated).toMatch(/mix-blend-mode:\s*normal;/);
    const gated = ruleBody(/@media \(prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference\)/);
    const blends = [...gated.matchAll(/mix-blend-mode:\s*([a-z-]+)/g)].map((match) => match[1]);
    expect(blends, "the motion gate blends nothing").toEqual(["normal"]);
  });

  it("keeps the still foil's overlay, which never moves (#1700)", () => {
    const still = ruleBody(/\.cf\[data-foil="static"\]::after,\s*\.cf\[data-foil="animated"\]::after/);
    expect(still).toMatch(/mix-blend-mode:\s*overlay/);
  });

  it("lights the swept band at SWEPT_ALPHA_SHARE of the still band's alpha, stop for stop (#1700)", () => {
    const still = gradients()
      .filter((gradient) => /\(\s*115deg,/.test(gradient))
      .map(alphas);
    const swept = gradients()
      .filter((gradient) => /\(\s*90deg,/.test(gradient))
      .map(alphas);
    expect(swept, "a swept band per still band").toHaveLength(still.length);
    for (const [band, stops] of still.entries()) {
      const sweptStops = swept[band] ?? [];
      expect(sweptStops, `band ${String(band)}'s stops`).toHaveLength(stops.length);
      for (const [at, alpha] of stops.entries()) {
        expect(sweptStops[at], `band ${String(band)} stop ${String(at)}`).toBeCloseTo(alpha * SWEPT_ALPHA_SHARE, 5);
      }
    }
  });
```

The six existing tests stay as they are and must still pass. They pin the layer (`left: 0`, `width: 170%`), `will-change: transform`, the 8 s animation, the keyframes and the reduced-motion gate, so together with the first new test they are the structural proof of the cost: per face, the same single layer moved by transform, minus the blend.

