- `sh scripts/build-wasm.sh` once (vitest's setup imports the wasm package; without it the file fails to load), then `pnpm --dir apps/web exec vitest run src/cards/foil.test.ts`. Expect 9 passed.
- `pnpm --dir apps/web typecheck`
- `pnpm exec eslint apps/web/src/cards/foil.test.ts`

## Done when

- [ ] Both `90deg` sweep gradients in `cards.css` have the alphas of steps 1–2, the gold sweep rule has `mix-blend-mode: normal;`, and the still foil rule, the keyframes and every other rule are byte-for-byte unchanged (`git diff` shows only those lines and the comment).
- [ ] `foil.test.ts` has the three new tests, and all 9 tests pass.
- [ ] The doc addendum is at the end of `docs/polish/6-cards.md`.
- [ ] Web typecheck and eslint are clean; the harness's web tests (vitest `--changed`) pass. No Rust changed, so the cargo checks have nothing new to catch, but they must still be green.

## Risks

- **Brightness drift.** Normal blending lifts a light backdrop less than overlay did, and a dark one about the same, so the band reads a touch softer on the gilded edge. Use the values given. Do not retune them by eye, and do not raise them past the still band's alpha (the third test holds the ratio).
